jobs.description:
Apex.AI is an international software company developing safety-certified, developer-friendly, and scalable software for mobility and autonomous systems. Our technology enables companies to build software-defined vehicles and intelligent machines faster, safer, and more efficiently.  &nbsp;  


  We are looking for a   hands-on  IT Administrator / (Senior) IT Administrator      to take ownership of the day-to-day operation and continuous improvement of our IT environment in Germany while supporting our international teams.  &nbsp;  


  This is a highly practical role for someone who enjoys solving technical problems, administering systems, supporting users, and continuously improving IT infrastructure. You will work across   Linux and macOS endpoints, identity and access management, cloud services, networks, security tooling, and on-premises infrastructure  .  &nbsp;  

  You will be a key point of contact for IT topics in our Munich office and work closely with Engineering, DevOps, HR, and other business functions.  &nbsp;  


  In addition to your core IT responsibilities, you will have the opportunity to   develop your knowledge of Information Security and compliance  , including ISO 27001 and TISAX. Previous compliance experience is welcome but   not required  —we are looking for someone who is interested in learning and growing in this area.  &nbsp;  


  As Apex.AI grows, this role offers the opportunity to take on broader ownership and help shape the future of our IT function.  &nbsp;  
 &nbsp; 
  This role is located in our Munich office. Authorization to work in Germany is required.  

   What You’ll Do   


   Hands-on IT Administration  &nbsp;   




  Own and manage the day-to-day operation of our cloud and on-premises IT environment.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Administer and support   Linux and macOS endpoints   throughout their lifecycle.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Manage MDM, IAM, user accounts, permissions, SSO, and MFA.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Administer cloud-based email, collaboration, and file-storage services.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Manage employee access across internal systems and business applications.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Configure, maintain, and troubleshoot wired and wireless networks.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Manage VPN solutions, network segmentation, policies, and access rules.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Administer and maintain on-premises and cloud-based servers.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  








  Manage endpoint security solutions, including EDR/antivirus, patching, encryption, and security policies.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Implement and maintain integrations between different IT systems.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Automate repetitive IT administration tasks wherever possible.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Monitor systems and proactively identify and resolve issues before they impact users.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  




   IT Support &amp; Service Delivery  &nbsp;   




  Be a primary point of contact for IT support for employees in our Munich office and provide remote support to colleagues in other locations.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Troubleshoot hardware, software, endpoint, network, account, and access issues.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Manage IT support requests and ensure issues are resolved efficiently.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Set up laptops, accounts, permissions, and required applications for new employees.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Execute IT onboarding and offboarding for employees and contractors.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Manage IT hardware inventory and device lifecycle.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Maintain clear and useful technical documentation.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Help create a reliable and user-friendly IT environment where employees can work effectively with minimal friction.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  




   IT Security &amp; Compliance  &nbsp;   


  You will have the opportunity to learn

